cff-version: 1.2.0
title: A segmentation and tracking pipeline for budding yeast microfluidics movies
message: >-
  If you use this pipeline in work that is published, please cite it using the
  metadata in this file, and cite the underlying tools it depends on - YeaZ,
  btrack and MIDAP - separately. Their references are listed under
  "references" below.
type: software
version: v0.1.0
date-released: 2026
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22871367

authors:
  # Software: wrote the original pipeline - the segmentation step, splitting the
  # movie by trap, formatting for midap, tracking, the mother-cell heuristic and
  # the fluorescence extraction (ETH Zurich, Scientific IT Services, 2023-2024).
  - given-names: Nadia
    family-names: Marounina
    email: nmarounina@ethz.ch
    # TODO: ask Nadia to add her ORCID.
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'

  # Conceptualisation, biological input, validation and testing; and the later
  # development of the pipeline from mid-2024 onwards (ETH Zurich, Institute of
  # Biochemistry, 2023-2025).
  - given-names: Tom
    family-names: Peskett
    email: thomaspeskett@googlemail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2008-688X'

  # Software: wrote the template matching routine (template_matching.py).
  # Supervision of the computational side of the project.
  - given-names: Tarun
    family-names: Chadha
    website: 'https://github.com/chadhat'
    # TODO: ask Tarun for his ORCID.
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'

# Point of contact for questions about the pipeline, bug reports and requests to
# reuse it. This is separate from authorship above: it says who to write to, not
# who did the work.
contact:
  - given-names: Tom
    family-names: Peskett
    email: thomaspeskett@googlemail.com

abstract: >-
  A data analysis pipeline for time-lapse microscopy of budding yeast held in
  microfluidic traps. It takes a stack of bright-field and fluorescence TIFF
  images and produces, for each trap, a cropped and drift-corrected movie, a
  per-cell segmentation, cell tracks, a heuristic identification of the mother
  cell, and the fluorescence trace of that mother cell over time.

keywords:
  - yeast
  - budding yeast
  - replicative ageing
  - time-lapse microscopy
  - microfluidics
  - cell segmentation
  - cell tracking
  - image analysis

license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/TRPeskett/yeast_segtrack_pipeline'

